{
  "statement": "Safety and reliability are paramount in our bookkeeping system. Requirements SAF-01 (accurate transaction recording) and SAF-02 (double-entry principles) are essential to prevent data loss and discrepancies. SAF-03 (audit trail retention) ensures accountability and historical integrity. SAF-04 (error handling) is crucial for managing faults during processing, while SAF-05 (safe degradation) allows essential functions during outages. SAF-06 (currency conversion validation) prevents financial discrepancies, and SAF-07 (regular backups) mitigates data loss risks. However, I raise conflicts with TRU-01 as encryption may complicate our ability to accurately record transactions, and with EFF-07, as logging delays could hinder auditing processes.",
